{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqb1i6ssdft","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Gate label pipeline: nightly labeler joins journal rows to task outcomes","summary":"Design (2026-06-12) for the MISSING piece of the gate flywheel — outcome linkage. The gate journal logs features at decision time; labels arrive later from outcomes. Build scripts/gate-label.js, run in nightly QA: read unlabeled gate-journal.jsonl rows, join each to its task's terminal state via key (workspace, task_key, ts-window), emit a labeled row to gate-labeled.jsonl. Four-quadrant label (from [[note-mqasdxx0tnt]]): inject+note-used+pass=TP; inject+note-NOT-referenced=FP (regardless of pass); abstain+pass=TN; abstain+fail+post-hoc KB note matches root cause=FN. note-used = lexical proxy: injected topKey or high note-content-token overlap appears in the task transcript or produced artifact (validated against paired bench arms). FN = post-mortem matcher: embed the failed task root cause, search KB AS-OF fail time, match above threshold => FN. Label v1 = binary helped/not; v2 = cost-aware utility (outcome_delta - lambda*cost_delta) sample-weighting once lambda measured from paired ON/OFF bench arms. Filter rows by embedModel (drift guard). Log label-coverage (rows labeled vs pending) for selection-bias visibility. Data is off-policy logged-bandit, not dirty. Extends [[note-mqaslontp50]].","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T14:46:47.020Z","vec":[-0.04029633849859238,0.025152722373604774,-0.06466364115476608,0.031433336436748505,-0.001654276973567903,-0.005522498860955238,-0.01666765660047531,-0.009786341339349747,-0.003977408166974783,-0.0895143523812294,-0.07896531373262405,-0.004421730991452932,-0.04397689178586006,0.015765666961669922,0.00041820137994363904,-0.005136572755873203,0.016692595556378365,-0.04212871193885803,0.023039424791932106,-0.09527479112148285,-0.042871180921792984,0.04499409720301628,0.07119061052799225,0.04695911705493927,-0.03575081750750542,-0.00335384